0. Talty, Empire of Blue Water, p.172. He cites many reasons why the Spanish had a difficult time in 
defeating Morgan, which includes the huge distances of the Spanish Main that made it virtually 
impossible to defend far-flung cities, inadequate weapons, lack of money for new armament, 
reliance on militias mostly created from local people and not trained professionals, bureaucracy 
that stifled initiative, bickering provincial governors and many more. 


